                "entry_id": "3259e020-1b2b-3271-affa-cd9cf35022ed",
                "word": "truculence",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "e649bf09-11c7-435c-810e-28a80f67f801",
                        "entry_id": "3259e020-1b2b-3271-affa-cd9cf35022ed",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "truculences"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "569a44a1-7ac4-357c-a917-da12b8f3acd8",
                        "entry_id": "3259e020-1b2b-3271-affa-cd9cf35022ed",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The state of being truculent; eagerness to fight; ferocity."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable",
                            "usually"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "94cda226-63e4-4486-8860-ad7897787d10",
                                "sense_id": "569a44a1-7ac4-357c-a917-da12b8f3acd8",
                                "text": "To these provincial autocrats, before whom the peaceable population of all classes had been accustomed to tremble, the reserve of that English-looking engineer caused an uneasiness which swung to and fro between cringing and truculence."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f6c8dfd1-5721-4ad7-83b1-44ddc7e3163d",
                                "sense_id": "569a44a1-7ac4-357c-a917-da12b8f3acd8",
                                "text": "He was huge in all that he did, and his benevolence was even more overpowering than his truculence."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fec8a217-1112-4b72-9d4a-52d91cfa8e43",
                                "sense_id": "569a44a1-7ac4-357c-a917-da12b8f3acd8",
                                "text": "Dundy’s fists were clenched in front of his body and his feet were planted firm and a little apart on the floor, but the truculence in his face was modified by thin rims of white showing between green irises and upper eyelids."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "228bfe69-38b1-4a5f-b26a-6c2beda98c97",
                                "sense_id": "569a44a1-7ac4-357c-a917-da12b8f3acd8",
                                "text": "Trump’s truculence on the world stage: “Everyone kowtows to Iran because they’re crazy. Now we have our own bit of crazy.”"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
